 "summary": "The new Frobenius lemmas (f = order of the residue Frobenius, f \u2223 orderOf \u03c3, f = 1 \u2194 \u03c3 \u2208 I(Q)) are correct at ramified primes, and the multiquadratic criterion checks out against \u211a(\u221a3,\u221a6), \u211a(\u221a3,\u221a21), \u211a(\u221a3,\u221a-6) and \u211a(i,\u221a3); the i = j case of the pair condition is true rather than contradictory, and the 2^(n-2) count has no satisfiable n = 1 instance. The ResidueDegree generalisation to g \u00b7 2^k = [K:\u211a] is sound without Nonempty \u03b9.",
